{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1318872-question-on-mta","id":1318872,"title":"Question on MtA","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-06-16T09:08:35-07:00","id":1318872,"title":"Question on MtA","content":"Hi. Just checking into MtA since I really find the setting interesting. But I was wondering do mages have the ability to astral project ie leave their bodies and that kind of thing? Just morbid curiosity while I wait on my copy of the rulebook.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/993-munkieboi","name":"munkieboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar993_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-16T09:15:16-07:00","id":1318876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>munkieboi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1318872-question-on-mta#post1318872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi. Just checking into MtA since I really find the setting interesting. But I was wondering do mages have the ability to astral project ie leave their bodies and that kind of thing? Just morbid curiosity while I wait on my copy of the rulebook.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, at Mind 3 they can use the spell to project into the Mind attuned frequency of Twilight. And every mage can meditate their way into their dreams, soul or the collective unconscious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-16T10:49:15-07:00","id":1318896,"title":"","content":"Cool. Thanks for the info. Already got a handful of ideas for scenarios for the game. That just makes some more viable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/993-munkieboi","name":"munkieboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar993_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-16T12:41:14-07:00","id":1318926,"title":"","content":"PDFs are quicker and cheaper if you don't hate them.<br /> <br /> If they're okay, I recommend grabbing the 1st edition book called Astral Realms. SO fun! So much astral projecting! Its relatively cheap in pdf form","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-16T13:09:04-07:00","id":1318929,"title":"","content":"Yep, the Astral Realms are just <i>the best thing ever</i>. Easily my favourite part of Mage. There's so much stuff you can encounter, and the deeper you go, the weirder it gets.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-16T13:42:50-07:00","id":1318937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1318872-question-on-mta?p=1318926#post1318926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">PDFs are quicker and cheaper if you don't hate them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not a fan of PDFs for main rulebooks. Just old fashioned that way. But other stuff np. Will check out astral realms you mentioned. Wierd stuff is always cool imo. I'm usually really good with wierd metaphysical psychedelic stuff. Thanks. Is there a list of mage published stuff I could look over to see what I want to add to my game anywhere?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/993-munkieboi","name":"munkieboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar993_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-16T13:44:09-07:00","id":1318938,"title":"","content":"Also depending on what you actually want from astral projection, you just can use Spirit/Death magic to make yourself intangible, no need to leave a body lying around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-16T14:43:17-07:00","id":1318947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>munkieboi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1318872-question-on-mta?p=1318937#post1318937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not a fan of PDFs for main rulebooks. Just old fashioned that way. But other stuff np. Will check out astral realms you mentioned. Wierd stuff is always cool imo. I'm usually really good with wierd metaphysical psychedelic stuff. Thanks. Is there a list of mage published stuff I could look over to see what I want to add to my game anywhere?</div> </div> </div> </div>What are you looking for? My bias is clear, I like critters. So I'd recommend Intruders, encounters with the abyss, as well as Summoners. Outside of Beast, the Astral is the only mage-specific phenomenon that can be easily encountered. (pending signs of sorcery, thats not out yet). So Astral Realms and the core will have you covered for awhile. Focus on your passions first Id say, and spread out as things become stale.<br /> <br /> But, when book recommendations come up you'll hear a lot of &quot;Get the Seers book&quot; and they're right if you're going to cover the Seers of the Throne or do Exarch stuff. The Seers book is almost paranoia inducing its so good.<br /> <br /> Also, avoid Imperial Mysteries for awhile, you might want it eventually but if you are new its going to be more fun to be blissfully unaware of what Archmages can do. Imperial Mysteries is great but it kinda deflates how the regular game feels if you read it too soon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-16T15:31:56-07:00","id":1318954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>munkieboi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1318872-question-on-mta?p=1318937#post1318937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a list of mage published stuff I could look over to see what I want to add to my game anywhere?</div> </div> </div> </div>DrivethruRPG has them all. Even if you're not buying PDFs, it at least gives you a complete list.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-16T18:16:28-07:00","id":1318989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1318872-question-on-mta?p=1318954#post1318954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">DrivethruRPG has them all. Even if you're not buying PDFs, it at least gives you a complete list.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perfect. Just want to know what's available and what it's about so I can add to my game as it grows and mutates as most of my games do. Don't want to just start grabbing random stuff that doesn't help at the time ya know? Thanks to Scarlet Witch for the direction. Seems like we're similar in tastes","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/993-munkieboi","name":"munkieboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar993_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-17T00:50:23-07:00","id":1319019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1318872-question-on-mta?p=1318876#post1318876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, at Mind 3 they can use the spell to project into the Mind attuned frequency of Twilight.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just a quick correction, Psychic Projection is actually Mind 4.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-17T05:18:34-07:00","id":1319034,"title":"","content":"Also, another technical correction, the Astral realms are something completely different in Mage than what most people understand as astral projection. As such, Mage doesn't HAVE astral projection, not as such. As others have stated you can achieve similar results, but the word Astral is reserved for the Astral Realms, since it's, you know, a Thing. For that reason alone I'd recommend getting the Astral realms book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-17T09:35:23-07:00","id":1319068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Falcon777</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1318872-question-on-mta?p=1319034#post1319034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, another technical correction, the Astral realms are something completely different in Mage than what most people understand as astral projection. As such, Mage doesn't HAVE astral projection, not as such. As others have stated you can achieve similar results, but the word Astral is reserved for the Astral Realms, since it's, you know, a Thing. For that reason alone I'd recommend getting the Astral realms book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the clarification. I'll definitely put it on the top of my to get list. Just seems to me that astral projection and magic should go together. But I did read a lot of those time-life occult books as a kid...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/993-munkieboi","name":"munkieboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar993_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-17T10:54:26-07:00","id":1319083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Falcon777</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1318872-question-on-mta?p=1319034#post1319034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, another technical correction, the Astral realms are something completely different in Mage than what most people understand as astral projection. As such, Mage doesn't HAVE astral projection, not as such. As others have stated you can achieve similar results, but the word Astral is reserved for the Astral Realms, since it's, you know, a Thing. For that reason alone I'd recommend getting the Astral realms book.</div> </div> </div> </div>What do most people think of it as then? When I first read the book I was blown away by how &quot;accurate&quot; it was, or how much it fit to what I'd expected and hoped.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-17T10:54:48-07:00","id":1319084,"title":"","content":"There are a lot of additional ways to project your senses beyond simply leaving your body behind. There's the classic Scrying for instance, or you could perhaps cast an Unveiling Life spell on a bird to see what it sees as it flies around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-17T11:17:32-07:00","id":1319089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1318872-question-on-mta?p=1319084#post1319084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are a lot of additional ways to project your senses beyond simply leaving your body behind. There's the classic Scrying for instance, or you could perhaps cast an Unveiling Life spell on a bird to see what it sees as it flies around.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what I think makes the setting so interesting. The many ways to skin the cat approach to accomplishing a lot of things. Astral projection I feel is a classic way to extend your senses to percieve things otherwise inpercivable. Similar to scrying it's a classic trope of genres with magic","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/993-munkieboi","name":"munkieboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar993_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-17T12:49:01-07:00","id":1319107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1318872-question-on-mta?p=1319083#post1319083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do most people think of it as then? When I first read the book I was blown away by how &quot;accurate&quot; it was, or how much it fit to what I'd expected and hoped.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a bit confusing. A lot of people use it to mean something like remote-viewing or out-of-body experiences, your soul or astral form floats around the world whilst your physical body stays where it is. I gather it's a meaning that comes from Theosophy as opposed to older ideas that involved the soul flying off into mystical realms.<br /> <br /> That said, it seems more recent magician types tend to blend the two ideas together.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-17T13:04:25-07:00","id":1319110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1318872-question-on-mta?p=1319083#post1319083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What do most people think of it as then? When I first read the book I was blown away by how &quot;accurate&quot; it was, or how much it fit to what I'd expected and hoped.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most people see Astral projection as moving your mind/soul out of yourself and floating around like a ghost (intangible, possibly visible (though not always), not necessarily anchored, able to view the material world with no difficulty, move through walls, etc). Think of what the Ancient one did to Banner Hulk in Endgame. The Astral Realms aren't like that at all. Not really.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-17T15:48:13-07:00","id":1319139,"title":"","content":"Psychic Projection (Mind 4) for the out-of-body interpretation, and the Astral Realms for the spiritual journey/visiting mystical realms interpretation. I think all bases are covered.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-17T15:54:11-07:00","id":1319141,"title":"","content":"Watch the Doctor Strange movie, the parts where he and others are travelling about unseen, passing through walls and fighting it out, are an example of Twilight Projection.<br /> The part where the Ancient sends him flying through realms of hands and Dommoro, that is Astral Space.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}